1
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,420
Madoka just has the worst luck...

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:08,460
...coming down with a cold 
right before our family trip.

3
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,040
M-my fever finally broke.

4
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:16,580
But it's too late now...

5
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:19,250
I really wanted to go to Fiji.

6
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:23,040
Please hold down the fort
while we're away for Golden Week.
- The Family

7
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:22,130
And now I'm stuck here for a whole week.

8
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:25,460
I don't know if I can survive all alone...

9
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:30,170
That futon has legs!

10
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:52,000
Rikukaikuu doko ni ikou
Where to go? The land, sea or sky?

11
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:54,580
Ahiru no Sora

12
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:55,040
Kimi o sasoitai na
I wanna invite you to come along

13
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:59,880
Monogatari wa hajima tterunda
The pages of our story have started to turn

14
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:05,630
Okubyou kaze mo recycle
If you lose your nerve then recycle it

15
00:01:05,630 --> 00:01:08,630
Mayotteru senaka oshite
And let it push you past hesitation

16
00:01:08,630 --> 00:01:13,830
Give and go! Isogou
Give and go! With the flow

17
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:21,960
Mogutteita honou ga kaodashite
Instincts that are buried deep will always rear their head again

18
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:29,170
Kakusenai no sa yume ni mita yume
People can't just hide the dreams they once dreamed of

19
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:32,580
Tobenai tsubasa demo
Even if these wings can't fly

20
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:39,420
Bokura wa habataite sora o kanjitai
We want to spread them wide and embrace the sky

21
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,750
Naritai jibun ni naritai
Becoming the people who we want to be

22
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:49,460
Ima dekinai koto mo ashita wa wakannai ze
You never know, the impossible could be possible tomorrow

23
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:52,920
Waru agaki shiyou
So let's keep up the struggle

24
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,960
Happy go ducky!

25
00:02:06,210 --> 00:02:07,920
It's... too heavy!

26
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,080
Hey! You're late, Kurumatani.

27
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:12,130
Differing Enthusiasm

28
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:12,130
Dude, you lugged that thing all the way here?

29
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:13,330
Nanao Sports

30
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,330
Good morning!

31
00:02:16,330 --> 00:02:18,460
Whoa, that's a lot of luggage!

32
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:20,000
Allow me to assist you.

33
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,250
Oh... thank you!

34
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:25,210
Hey, Nao, these are from my dad.

35
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:27,290
Wow! So many veggies!

36
00:02:27,290 --> 00:02:29,710
They're fresh from our store.

37
00:02:29,710 --> 00:02:32,670
I didn't realize that your family
ran a grocery store, Yashuara.

38
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:37,040
Yeah, and Nabe's old man 
runs a farm down in Ibaraki.

39
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:38,460
Here's 20 kilos of rice.

40
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:40,630
Whoa, incredible!

41
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:44,210
Okay, then, I know this isn't
much of a thank you, but please...

42
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:45,710
...take these.

43
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:47,330
F-for us?

44
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:50,630
They were our display pieces, 
so they're not the cleanest.

45
00:02:50,630 --> 00:02:52,880
Sweet! A perfect fit!

46
00:02:53,290 --> 00:02:56,770
Since basketball puts a 
lot of strain on the legs,

47
00:02:56,770 --> 00:03:00,030
I thought you guys should have proper shoes.

48
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:03,710
I think I want get married to Nao...!

49
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:05,960
Where are we gonna be sleeping?

50
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,540
And also eat our meals.

51
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,880
You'll all be sleeping in the gym, obviously.

52
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:12,540
We have permission to use the Home Ec classroom
for cooking and eating.

53
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:15,080
So then, where will you sleep, Nao?

54
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:18,500
Mr. Satsuki unlocked the break room for me,
but to be honest...

55
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,960
...I'm scared of sleeping by myself,
so I'll stay with all of you.

56
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:25,830
WITH ALL OF US?!

57
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,880
This is the best training camp ever!

58
00:03:30,250 --> 00:03:33,170
Okay everybody, get changed 
and then meet in the gym!

59
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:34,330
ROGER!

60
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:38,880
Yoko:
Did you get over your cold?

61
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,830
Yoko:
Did you get over your cold?
Yoko:
I hear the boys' team is doing a training camp right now.

62
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,130
A training camp?

63
00:03:39,830 --> 00:03:41,210
Yoko:
I hear the boys' team is doing a training camp right now.

64
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,880
That sounds like a lot of fun!

65
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:47,710
I thought that we'd end up
doing intense training all day, but...

66
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:50,080
This might actually be fun,
like one of those seaside schools!

67
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,920
I brought a console for us to play with.

68
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:55,630
The Legend of Rails

69
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,420
Nice, Yasu!

70
00:03:53,420 --> 00:03:55,540
I guess we're having a game tourney tonight!

71
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:56,830
Chiaki's Notes

72
00:03:56,380 --> 00:04:01,210
From what I've uncovered,
Nao's grades in Home Ec are at the top of her class.

73
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:02,080
Awesome!

74
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:04,380
I'm looking forward to see 
what she cooks us for dinner!

75
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:05,830
I thought they might get bummed out
at the idea of a training camp,

76
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:06,710
Yeah, I'm curious to see what it'll be!

77
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:08,130
but it looks like everyone
will be in good spirits for practice.

78
00:04:08,130 --> 00:04:11,290
Is there anybody who wouldn't be excited
for an event like this?

79
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:14,960
There's something even more amazing
waiting for us after dinner.

80
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,040
Oh?!

81
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,540
And what makes you say that?

82
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:20,380
Because I've already worked 
my magic on the baths.

83
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:23,540
You really do have all of 
your bases covered, man!

84
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,460
Training camps for the win!

85
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:31,040
Oh, they're really going at it.

86
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:33,460
Hey, guys!

87
00:04:33,460 --> 00:04:35,250
I came to hang out!

88
00:04:41,710 --> 00:04:43,630
They're all totally wiped out...

89
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:47,630
...and there isn't even a ball on the court.
Have they just been running?!

90
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:55,630
What's going on Nao?

91
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,250
Oh, hello, Madoka.

92
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:59,670
I heard you guys were doing 
a training camp, but...

93
00:04:59,670 --> 00:05:02,330
Yep. We just got started today.

94
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:05,040
You just started and they're 
already this tired?

95
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,080
Yes.

96
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,750
The emphasis of this training is on footwork,
so it's extra difficult for the three newbies.

97
00:05:10,330 --> 00:05:14,540
But for our experienced members,
I'm making them do double what those three are.

98
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:18,250
The most important thing for them right now
is to build stamina and toughen up.

99
00:05:18,250 --> 00:05:19,630
Running
Time based (20 mins) or Laps outside (30 times)
Stretches
Full court dash
Backwards run
Dash and Stop
Hands up
Jump
Leg Bounce
Shuttle Run
Ladder (20 times x 10 sets)

100
00:05:18,710 --> 00:05:21,920
Y-you're making them do all this in one day?

101
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:21,380
Skipping
Thigh Lifts
Side Kicks
Leg Bounces
Two Leg Jumps
Slide Steps
Mirror Dribble (zig-zag)
No Ball
Side Step
Cross Step
Side Step

102
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:22,710
Dribble Practice
Front back dribble
Left right dribble
High low dribble
2 players  (50 times)
3 players (50 times)
Half 1-on-1 (20 times)
Match Practice
Shooting Practice

103
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:25,380
We had no morning practice today,
so this was on the easy end.

104
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:26,670
Sleep

105
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:29,710
In addition to that, I've set aside
individual practice time for everyone

106
00:05:26,670 --> 00:05:27,420
Sleep | Running/Stretches

107
00:05:27,420 --> 00:05:28,170
Sleep | Running/Stretches | Breakfast

108
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:28,920
Sleep | Running/Stretches | Breakfast | Morning Practice

109
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:29,670
Sleep | Running/Stretches | Breakfast | Morning Practice
Lunch

110
00:05:29,670 --> 00:05:30,420
Sleep | Running/Stretches | Breakfast | Morning Practice
Lunch | Afternoon Practice

111
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:32,630
to work on refining their 
skills in the evenings.

112
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:31,170
Sleep | Running/Stretches | Breakfast | Morning Practice
Lunch | Afternoon Practice | Dinner

113
00:05:31,170 --> 00:05:32,630
Sleep | Running/Stretches | Breakfast | Morning Practice
Lunch | Afternoon Practice | Dinner | Individual Practice

114
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:38,880
Right now, this is nothing
but a gathering of talented players.

115
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:42,460
They're still completely 
undeveloped as a team.

116
00:05:43,790 --> 00:05:45,790
The entire point of this training camp...

117
00:05:45,790 --> 00:05:49,000
...is to create the real 
Kuzu High basketball team.

118
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:52,140
A team that will survive 
the intense competition

119
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:55,290
of the Kanagawa block and go 
to the inter-high tournament.

120
00:05:55,580 --> 00:06:00,210
I believe with all of my heart,
that these guys are capable of that.

121
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,790
I can tell, she's serious about this...

122
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:07,170
When you've finished with that, 
please go and walk it off!

123
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:10,330
Get your breathing under control
and then start pushing your pace up!

124
00:06:13,170 --> 00:06:14,750
They're like zombies.

125
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:19,000
But it's hard to believe that until recently,
all these guys did was get into fights.

126
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,500
Hey, Nao?

127
00:06:24,290 --> 00:06:26,920
Is there are anything 
that I can help out with?

128
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:27,920
Huh?

129
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:32,880
My house is totally empty now,
so I wouldn't mind staying overnight.

130
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:35,210
Really? That would be a big help!

131
00:06:35,210 --> 00:06:38,250
Um, in that case, I do have 
one favor to ask of you.

132
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,630
Sure. Anything you want!

133
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:54,920
Home Ec. Room

134
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,580
That's a hard pass, even from me.

135
00:06:57,580 --> 00:06:59,880
For real, my stomach
isn't accepting any donations right now.

136
00:07:02,710 --> 00:07:05,540
Those jerks! After all 
that effort I put in...

137
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:08,170
Though I will admit I 
screwed up just a little.

138
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:13,670
Seconds, please. I'm still hungry.

139
00:07:13,670 --> 00:07:16,540
You don't have to force yourself 
to eat it on my account.

140
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:18,130
The hell are you going on about?

141
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:21,750
It's a little saltier than ordinary, 
but it tastes just fine.

142
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:25,500
Thanks...

143
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,920
And so, the first one bites the dust...

144
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,630
Survival of the fittest.

145
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:37,830
RIP in peace, Momoharu.

146
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,880
What now? Should we play games or something?

147
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:45,380
My muscles are so cramped 
that I can't move an inch.

148
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:46,830
Let's just sleep.

149
00:07:47,210 --> 00:07:48,670
Hold your horses, gentlemen.

150
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,080
There's still one thing left...

151
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:54,170
...the main event of this evening.

152
00:07:57,630 --> 00:07:59,710
Ah, this feels great!

153
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,880
Are you really sure this is okay?

154
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,080
Huh?

155
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,380
Spending your holiday with 
us at the training camp.

156
00:08:05,580 --> 00:08:07,290
I have nothing better to do.

157
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:09,250
This is one good way to pass the time.

158
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:12,960
Plus, just think, it would be dangerous for you
to be here alone.

159
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:14,710
Those guys are wild animals.

160
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:17,960
To be honest, I did have my 
own worries about that...

161
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:25,040
But there's something else.

162
00:08:26,790 --> 00:08:29,380
One more thing I'm really concerned about.

163
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:31,710
I've amassed a lot of basketball knowledge,

164
00:08:31,710 --> 00:08:34,240
but that's not enough to 
make me a proper coach.

165
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:37,460
I've been putting up a facade of confidence
in front of everyone until now.

166
00:08:39,170 --> 00:08:42,710
But I'm not really sure if what we're doing
will actually work in the end.

167
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:46,020
Alternatively, I know that 
if I seem hesitant at all,

168
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:48,210
then it will just cause 
everyone to have doubts.

169
00:08:48,630 --> 00:08:52,460
I've already prepared myself for the worst
if they end up hating me for it, but...

170
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:55,290
You're doing just fine. No problem.

171
00:08:56,460 --> 00:09:00,210
I think everyone is already aware
of what they need to do to better themselves.

172
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:04,710
Plus, I get the feeling that brave face you put on
is getting through to them.

173
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,880
Shhh!

174
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:12,540
Listen up, I jammed a small rock
into the bottom of this window earlier.

175
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:16,000
Now it won't fully close
and gets stuck open just a tiny bit.

176
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:18,540
Your foresight is most admirable, commander!

177
00:09:21,250 --> 00:09:23,830
Great. Then I shall take the first peek!

178
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:29,630
Whew, I'm feeling refreshed!

179
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:32,790
Fuji Bathhouse
Sauna
Electric Bath
Whirlpool Jet Bath

180
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:32,790
It's really nice to have a bathhouse
so close to where the school is.

181
00:09:32,790 --> 00:09:34,330
Wh-what's wrong, Chiaki?!

182
00:09:34,330 --> 00:09:36,210
Ugh, they got me.

183
00:09:36,210 --> 00:09:38,420
What do you mean? Who got you?!

184
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:41,960
I dunno! Some sort of mysterious creature
that I've never seen before!

185
00:09:46,170 --> 00:09:48,380
Come on! Hurry up, Sora!

186
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:50,290
Here!

187
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:52,790
M-Madoka...

188
00:09:58,330 --> 00:10:00,420
Wait up, Madoka...!

189
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:03,290
You're walking too fast...!

190
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:11,290
First, a 7.5-kilometer run.

191
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:14,080
I sure had a nice dream.

192
00:10:15,790 --> 00:10:19,210
Afterwards, an hour of 
stretches and loosening up.

193
00:10:19,380 --> 00:10:22,000
Following breakfast, we 
get into morning practice.

194
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:25,790
For the first half of the day,
our practice focuses entirely on footwork.

195
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:35,710
Greased
Lightning

196
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:39,920
I'm starting to think he 
might not even be human...

197
00:10:39,920 --> 00:10:43,130
Shit! What the hell do we 
gotta do to move like he does?

198
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:46,080
All we've been doing is tripping 
up over and over again.

199
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:49,330
It's because your knees and toes
aren't properly pointed in the same direction.

200
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:54,580
You can't exert all the power that your legs
are capable of if you're off-balance.

201
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:58,080
It prevents you from running faster
and stopping more precisely.

202
00:10:58,710 --> 00:11:01,220
If you overpronate or get your 
knees pointed the wrong way,

203
00:11:01,220 --> 00:11:02,590
then you have to correct it right away.

204
00:11:02,790 --> 00:11:05,960
When you turn, you should carry your weight
on the ball of your foot.

205
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:12,040
I think their teamwork will develop nicely
if things keep progressing like this.

206
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:14,540
Aight, time for another set.

207
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:17,330
Hold up a sec! Let me rest for a bit!

208
00:11:17,630 --> 00:11:19,580
Cut the crap, you can't be that worn out.

209
00:11:19,580 --> 00:11:22,420
My feet hurt too much to run, dude.

210
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:23,670
I understand.

211
00:11:23,670 --> 00:11:26,080
Then the two of you can leave the court
and rest for a while.

212
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,580
We can't have anybody pushing so hard
that they break a bone or pass out.

213
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:30,420
Yeah!

214
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:31,500
All right!

215
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:32,460
However!

216
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:36,830
You will both be required to hold a ball
the entire time you're resting.

217
00:11:36,830 --> 00:11:39,130
I want the three of you, including Yasuhara,

218
00:11:39,330 --> 00:11:44,040
to do that at any time when you're
not actively practicing on the court. Okay?

219
00:11:51,130 --> 00:11:55,540
Whew, I'm super glad that Nanao was the one
who made dinner tonight.

220
00:11:56,040 --> 00:12:00,250
Ow! It's only the second day of our camp,
but my legs are already killing me.

221
00:12:00,580 --> 00:12:04,040
I don't think I'll last for 
1,000 shots of practice today.

222
00:12:08,630 --> 00:12:09,710
Kite...

223
00:12:15,250 --> 00:12:17,830
What's up? You here for solo practice, too?

224
00:12:17,830 --> 00:12:18,960
Oh, yeah!

225
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,880
Um, do you want me to throw you some passes?

226
00:12:24,330 --> 00:12:25,250
No need.

227
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:28,710
You have your own skills that you need
to stay focused on.

228
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:31,680
Don't spend your time fussing over others.

229
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:34,150
Work on improving your shot accuracy instead.

230
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:39,380
I shouldn't fuss over others, huh?

231
00:12:40,250 --> 00:12:44,460
But Kite is the one who spends the most time
fussing over the others during practice.

232
00:12:49,330 --> 00:12:51,290
Dammit! I won't let him outdo me!

233
00:12:56,750 --> 00:13:00,750
I guess it's pretty silly of me
to tell HIM of all people to work on accuracy.

234
00:13:04,250 --> 00:13:09,000
Nope, I'm done! After just 200 shots
I can't even move anymore...

235
00:13:09,750 --> 00:13:13,080
Hey, tell me something.
What do you think about this team?

236
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,920
What do you mean?

237
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:17,210
Well, the high school that 
I was supposed to go to

238
00:13:17,210 --> 00:13:20,690
always recruited top players 
from around the country.

239
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,420
"Supposed to go to"?

240
00:13:23,670 --> 00:13:25,670
And the coach there was highly regarded, too.

241
00:13:26,210 --> 00:13:31,420
But despite all of that they've never become
the national champs. Not even once.

242
00:13:32,210 --> 00:13:37,000
When I consider that, I can't help
but wonder why I'm sticking with this team.

243
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:40,080
The inter-high... is so far from our grasp.

244
00:13:41,250 --> 00:13:42,540
Kite...

245
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:44,880
Oh, there he is.

246
00:13:45,130 --> 00:13:47,710
Yo Kite! Teach me some 
more about how to dribble!

247
00:13:47,710 --> 00:13:48,830
Hey, Yasuhara!

248
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:51,670
I see you're holding on to the ball
just like Nanao told you to.

249
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:52,580
Yep.

250
00:13:52,830 --> 00:13:55,210
But I don't get it, is 
there a point to all this?

251
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:58,040
It's so that you develop a 
better feel for the ball.

252
00:13:58,040 --> 00:13:59,170
"Better feel"?

253
00:13:59,170 --> 00:14:02,250
Though, I know it can be boring
just fiddling around with it all day like that.

254
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:04,210
I'll teach you something fun you can do.

255
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:07,380
Trace the edge of the ball 
with your hand, like this.

256
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,750
Then stop it on the back of your hand.

257
00:14:09,290 --> 00:14:11,500
Repeat that in a loop 
with both of your hands.

258
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:14,080
Whoa! Dude, that's awesome!

259
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,880
It's called a "flip."

260
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:20,500
Whoops!

261
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:23,420
I can do it, too!

262
00:14:27,460 --> 00:14:30,130
So, hey. I think that you're right.

263
00:14:30,130 --> 00:14:32,630
The inter-high seems like
it's way out of our league right now.

264
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:36,080
But all we can really do is 
keep moving forward, right?

265
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:38,880
That's a good point.

266
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:42,830
I guess... everybody starts somewhere.

267
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:50,250
Man, I wasn't be able to 
do the flip at all today.

268
00:14:50,250 --> 00:14:52,790
It takes time, it's not meant to be easy.

269
00:14:52,790 --> 00:14:56,330
What's most important is that you spend
a lot of time handling the ball.

270
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:56,330
BOYS' BASKETBALL TEAM

271
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:01,080
And Chiaki goes down again!

272
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:02,040
Nooooo!

273
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:02,960
That sucks for you, dude!

274
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:03,830
Let's reset it.

275
00:15:03,830 --> 00:15:06,330
No way! That's a cheap move, cheater!

276
00:15:06,330 --> 00:15:08,170
Okay, fine then. Let's pick 
this up with a clean sla-

277
00:15:08,170 --> 00:15:11,710
You were too tired to run, but it looks like
you've got plenty of energy for games.

278
00:15:11,710 --> 00:15:12,710
Huh?

279
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:15,600
Didn't our manager give 
you an order to hold on

280
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:18,750
to a ball whenever you're 
not out on the court?

281
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:21,290
You got something to say, punk?

282
00:15:21,290 --> 00:15:24,420
It's called "free" time because we can spend it
doing whatever we want!

283
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,750
That ain't right.

284
00:15:26,330 --> 00:15:28,580
You guys need to double down 
and learn all the basics,

285
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:31,040
so that you can practice with the rest of us.

286
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,950
I can't tell what you guys are thinking,

287
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:36,950
but I'm dead set on getting 
our team to the inter-high.

288
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:41,170
So please just keep your shit together
and don't hold the rest of us back.

289
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:47,040
I'm not gonna lie, that kind 
of pissed me off just now.

290
00:15:48,830 --> 00:15:51,920
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Let's not fight guys!

291
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:54,540
I think you overstepped the 
line with that comment, Kite.

292
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:56,330
It's important to take a 
breather sometimes, right?

293
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,460
Come on, just apologize to them.

294
00:15:58,460 --> 00:15:59,670
Why should I?

295
00:16:00,040 --> 00:16:02,170
Everything I said was true and you know it.

296
00:16:02,170 --> 00:16:03,000
Kite!

297
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,460
What do you think?

298
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,500
About what?

299
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:09,250
Nanao specifically gave 
those three something to do.

300
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:11,790
But only one of them is taking it seriously.

301
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,630
The other two are off playing a game.

302
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:17,420
Not only that, but they slacked off
during afternoon practice.

303
00:16:18,250 --> 00:16:19,460
But that's...

304
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:23,290
"Slacked off"?!

305
00:16:23,290 --> 00:16:26,130
Our feet hurt like hell, so 
we stopped to get some rest!

306
00:16:26,130 --> 00:16:28,920
Your feet may hurt,
but you could still use your hands.

307
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:31,290
Why do you think Nanao told you
to keep holding on to the ball?

308
00:16:33,670 --> 00:16:36,750
We have no fucking idea what 
the purpose of all this is!

309
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:39,080
Hey! Please, let's stop this!

310
00:16:39,830 --> 00:16:42,330
Wh-what's going on in here?

311
00:16:45,210 --> 00:16:50,170
BOYS' BASKETBALL TEAM

312
00:16:54,750 --> 00:16:58,580
You need to quit thinking that everyone here
is on the same page about the inter-high.

313
00:16:59,670 --> 00:17:02,090
Those guys have barely started, they're only

314
00:17:02,090 --> 00:17:05,500
at the point where basketball 
seems pretty fun.

315
00:17:05,830 --> 00:17:08,710
I know full well what it's like 
to fail and be discouraged.

316
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:12,580
And these are exactly the sort of differences
that drive a wedge into the team.

317
00:17:13,420 --> 00:17:16,670
Not everybody plays the game
just to support somebody else.

318
00:17:16,670 --> 00:17:19,790
I don't want to hear anymore bullshit
about us "holding you back."

319
00:17:32,630 --> 00:17:34,580
Oh, good morning.

320
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:36,080
You're up early today.

321
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,830
I couldn't really sleep that well.

322
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:39,330
Because of yesterday?

323
00:17:39,330 --> 00:17:40,210
Yeah.

324
00:17:40,210 --> 00:17:43,130
I don't think anything that 
Chiaki said was wrong...

325
00:17:43,710 --> 00:17:47,170
...but even so, I feel the 
same way that Kite does.

326
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,700
When it comes to sports, having 
a desire to improve becomes

327
00:17:50,700 --> 00:17:52,630
really important the further you go.

328
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,420
I'm sorry.

329
00:17:57,420 --> 00:18:00,880
I should have taken more care
and considered how those two must feel...

330
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:04,000
Oh, no! It's nothing that 
you need to apologize about!

331
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,460
Hey, Tinytown!

332
00:18:05,670 --> 00:18:08,380
It's way too early in the morning
to be going around flirting, dude.

333
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:10,880
N-nobody around here has 
been doing any flirting!

334
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:13,880
Whatever, have you seen 
Nabe or Chucky around?

335
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:14,790
Huh?

336
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,790
I can't find them anywhere.

337
00:18:19,130 --> 00:18:22,000
All of their luggage is packed up and gone.

338
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:24,540
They made a break for it.

339
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:27,420
Hell yeah!

340
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:28,920
Awesome!

341
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:30,880
Kick ass!

342
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:31,880
I'm on fire!

343
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,420
You haven't won yet!

344
00:18:35,170 --> 00:18:37,130
What a haul!
That was genius! Pure genius!

345
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:41,460
Now THIS is what a vacation should be like!

346
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:44,580
Screw training camp.
Those guys who want to practice can go right ahead!

347
00:18:44,670 --> 00:18:45,670
That's not fair!

348
00:18:45,670 --> 00:18:47,750
We were the ones who got here first!

349
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:48,790
What's this? A fight?

350
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:50,040
That's right! That's right!

351
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:56,380
You twerps suck, so go find 
somewhere else to play.

352
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:56,380
That's unfair! Cut it out!

353
00:18:56,630 --> 00:19:00,040
Which means I'm willing to spend some time
weeding out the world's bullies.

354
00:19:00,330 --> 00:19:03,460
But mostly because those jerks remind me
of Kite and it's pissing me off.

355
00:19:03,790 --> 00:19:05,580
Hey there, you little punks!

356
00:19:05,790 --> 00:19:08,790
You're too old to be bullying 
elementary schoolers.

357
00:19:08,790 --> 00:19:10,250
There's no bullying going on here.

358
00:19:10,460 --> 00:19:13,460
They're the ones who lost
the wager game, fair and square.

359
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,170
"Wager game"?

360
00:19:15,420 --> 00:19:18,580
The basketball hoop in this park
is the only one in the neighborhood.

361
00:19:19,330 --> 00:19:22,090
Whenever there's a debate 
about who gets to use it,

362
00:19:22,090 --> 00:19:25,060
both sides settle it with 
a wager game of basketball.

363
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:27,960
And let me guess, you guys were the winners?

364
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:32,380
Yep. If they want to play, then they should 
practice and get good enough to win.

365
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:34,040
That doesn't seem entirely fair.

366
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:36,480
I definitely don't agree with the idea that

367
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:38,820
the better players are 
the more important ones.

368
00:19:42,210 --> 00:19:44,250
Hey, listen up, kiddos.

369
00:19:45,170 --> 00:19:47,230
If middle schoolers can 
take on elementary kids,

370
00:19:47,230 --> 00:19:49,200
then you have no problem 
with high schoolers. Right?

371
00:19:49,250 --> 00:19:52,460
That's fine, but can you 
old farts actually play?

372
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:55,210
Prepare to have your socks knocked off.

373
00:19:55,210 --> 00:19:57,330
And roll out the red carpet!

374
00:19:57,330 --> 00:19:59,460
We're members of the Kuzu 
High basketball team!

375
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:03,000
Let's go out and look for them.

376
00:20:03,210 --> 00:20:05,420
No way. Too much effort, man.

377
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:07,000
It's better to leave them be.

378
00:20:07,210 --> 00:20:09,710
They're only going to get in our way
if we let them loaf around here.

379
00:20:10,130 --> 00:20:11,290
But that's not...

380
00:20:11,630 --> 00:20:12,960
What did you think?

381
00:20:13,210 --> 00:20:14,040
Huh?

382
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:17,630
What did you think after you saw them
act like that yesterday?

383
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:19,750
Well, I...

384
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:23,670
...but even so, I feel the 
same way that Kite does.

385
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:32,000
Shinshiro Middle
8 points
Kuzu High

386
00:20:30,830 --> 00:20:33,790
Anybody who lacks true 
passion for the game won't

387
00:20:33,790 --> 00:20:36,170
get better no matter how much they practice.

388
00:20:36,790 --> 00:20:39,380
You should know that better than anyone else.

389
00:20:39,960 --> 00:20:41,210
Passion...

390
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:48,170
Are you guys seriously on a basketball team?

391
00:20:48,170 --> 00:20:50,250
You can hardly even dribble 
the ball properly!

392
00:20:50,250 --> 00:20:53,000
What the hell? How are 
you guys this damn good?

393
00:20:53,380 --> 00:20:54,540
What do you mean?

394
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:56,960
We've been playing basketball 
since first grade.

395
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:58,420
First grade?

396
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:02,210
Does that mean these kids have been
 playing basketball for more than six years?!

397
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:05,460
We want to get even better.

398
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:08,330
We can't afford to spend time playing 
with a bunch of little twerps.

399
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:13,420
So please just keep your shit together
and don't hold the rest of us back.

400
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:16,630
Basketball is a tough sport, 
don't sell it short.

401
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:20,750
Even if you found those two,
what are you planning to say to them?

402
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:23,320
"It doesn't matter if you're not motivated,

403
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:25,510
let's try our best to get 
to the inter-high together"?

404
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:28,210
Or maybe, "who cares about the inter-high,

405
00:21:28,210 --> 00:21:31,660
let's just have fun with it 
and play games along the way"?

406
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:32,500
Well?

407
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,380
No way...

408
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:37,830
You know I could never 
say any of that to them.

409
00:21:39,460 --> 00:21:42,250
I mean, you explained it perfectly earlier.

410
00:21:42,250 --> 00:21:45,880
Those two only think of basketball
as being pretty fun, right?

411
00:21:46,380 --> 00:21:51,420
But that means, it's possible they'll come to enjoy it
even more in the future. Isn't that true?

412
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,790
That's why, they can't just quit playing
because of a minor setback like this.

413
00:21:56,710 --> 00:21:59,790
I've decided. I'm going out 
to look for them right now!

414
00:22:15,330 --> 00:22:18,670
Doredake sora o miagetatte
It didn't matter how long you stared up at the sky

415
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:21,960
Boku wa tobenai to kimi wa itta
You always said that you would never be able to fly

416
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:25,170
Ato nankai te o nobaseba
One night I cried wondering how long it would take

417
00:22:25,330 --> 00:22:28,540
Todoku no darou to naita yoru
Until I could finally reach you with my hands

418
00:22:28,670 --> 00:22:32,040
Nigedasu koto ni nareteitte
Eventually I got used to just running away

419
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:35,330
Sore ga yowasa dato shitta ano hi
Until the day I realized that was a weakness

420
00:22:35,330 --> 00:22:39,540
Hajimeyou mata, kyou kara
So let's start it all over, right now

421
00:22:42,170 --> 00:22:48,170
Taisetsu na mono wa itsudemo soba ni atta
The things precious to us were always close at hand

422
00:22:48,170 --> 00:22:54,500
Bokura wa itsumo hitori janai donna toki mo
We are never completely alone at any time in our lives

423
00:22:54,500 --> 00:22:57,830
Toberu sa doko made mo kimi wa
The truth is that you can fly, wherever you want

424
00:22:57,830 --> 00:23:01,580
Dare yori tataku tataku habataite
Spreading your wings to go far higher than anyone else

425
00:23:01,790 --> 00:23:05,830
Nagashita namida no kazu dake
The more tears that you shed

426
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:07,790
Tsuyoku narunda
Then the stronger you become

427
00:23:07,790 --> 00:23:11,170
Tsubasa hiroge sekai o megutte
Let's use those wings to travel the world over

428
00:23:11,170 --> 00:23:14,750
Dare mo shiranai mirai o sagasou
And find a path to a future that no one knows about

429
00:23:14,750 --> 00:23:19,330
Zutto, zutto, zutto
Always, always, always

430
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:23,000
Aruite yukou saa, issho ni
Walking onwards, all of us together

431
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Towards Victory

432
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:34,330
Next time: "Towards Victory."

